# Trusted cloud devices

Dashbird cloud (`dashbird.jayhasty.com`) uses HTTP basic auth. **Only the device IDs listed in
`DASHBOARD_TRUSTED_DEVICE_IDS` (cloud `.env`) skip the password** — never weaken this to
“any device after login.”

Real device UUIDs live **only** in:

- cloud / local `.env` (`DASHBOARD_TRUSTED_DEVICE_IDS`)
- optional local-only rule `.cursor/rules/trusted-devices.local.mdc` (gitignored)

**Never commit real device UUIDs** to the public repo, docs, or client JS.

## Agent behavior

- Do **not** ask Jay for the cloud basic-auth password when working on trusted-device auth for
  devices already in `DASHBOARD_TRUSTED_DEVICE_IDS` / the local rule.
- Do **not** broaden passwordless access to other devices, IPs, or “trust on first login.”
- LAN `docker-compose.yml` stays **without** auth — this rule is cloud-only.
- One-time setup per device: bookmark `/auth/device-bind?did=<id>` after basic auth
  (see `docs/deploy-vultr.md`). Treat UUIDs as non-secret identifiers but still keep them
  out of git; binding requires the basic-auth password once.
